description:
FILED s539a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-13) -- the CAUSE of #3619.

Reproducer (scratch/s539a/pr/cz3.pl in the s539a worktree; needs IO-Compress-2.214-0/lib on @INC):
  use Test::More tests => 1;
  BEGIN { use_ok('IO::Compress::Gzip::Constants'); }
  my $n = 0;
  for my $index ( GZIP_MIN_HEADER_SIZE + 1 .. GZIP_MIN_HEADER_SIZE + GZIP_FEXTRA_HEADER_SIZE + 1) { $n++ }
  print "# extra loop count: $n\n";
perl: 3 (and 4 for the Name loop); PCL (main 24988e35): 1 and 1.  The same constants imported by `BEGIN { require X; X->import }` (pr/cz4.pl) are right on main: the static parse sees that spelling as a `use`, but not a `use_ok` call.  So each of cz-03zlib-v1.t's four header-truncation loops (Extra 3, Name 4, Comment 7, CRC 2 iterations in perl) runs ONCE: 12 x 6 = 72 rows never emitted, the file ends cleanly at 400 of 472.  146 test files under ~/.cpan/build use the `BEGIN { use_ok(...) }` shape.

RULED by the reviewing session (s541, rule 9a): the fact `a call of this sub imports from the module named by its first argument` is DATA declared with the sub (lib/Test/More.pm or a lib/PCL/Facts/ overlay, a marker on its forward declaration); the MECHANISM in Pl/ is keyed on the marker, never a name: a call, as a statement directly in a BEGIN block's body, of a sub carrying the marker, with a literal module name first, is treated FOR PARSE FACTS ONLY as `use MODULE LIST` at that position.  Outside BEGIN: no effect.  Non-literal first argument: no effect, no die.

The #2610 detector LOGS these sites but stays silent in announce mode: #4882.

=== DONE (s539a) ===
Built as ruled: `sub use_ok ($;@) :pcl_import_directive;` in lib/Test/More.pm (the data; an overlay may carry the same attribute and it joins the source's agreeing declaration -- _carry_import_directive; the fact is excluded from a prototype's shape key); Pl::Parser::_with_import_directive puts it on the record in the module walk; Pl::Parser2::_import_directive_uses (the mechanism, keyed on the fact) turns a BEGIN-body call with a literal module into `use M LIST` for _premerge_one_include (the same merge a `use` takes; the old loop body extracted, no second copy).  Shapes: NAME('M', LIST) alone or before || / or / && / and, paren-less NAME 'M', LIST.  Outside BEGIN / non-literal: no effect, no die.  docs/shipped-modules.md "The import-directive fact"; DECIDED ## s539a.  Generation v2-14800, artifacts regenerated (stamps only).
Guards: Pl/t/facts-overlay-01.t rows 12-18 (fixture Pl/t/lib/DirectiveFix.pm + its overlay + DirectiveConsts.pm; row 16 / 18 the real `BEGIN { use_ok(...) }`; row 17 the negative via the detector table); 12-14 16-18 fail on the base, 15 (no die) passes on both.
POPULATION: predicted per file with the tree's own reader + merge (scratch/s539a/m3/predict.pl over the board + wide lists): 19 files; board-population A/B (896 files, PERL5LIB per dist) 19 DIFF / 877 SAME / RCDIFF 0 = 17 predicted + 2 detector-table-only (Text-CSV 12_acc 66_formula: qualified Text::CSV::new / ::csv) ; 2 predicted that did not move (Sub-Uplevel 04 05: the file's own BEGIN glob alias of CORE::GLOBAL::caller is a local record the merge never overwrites).  Wide A/B 2,053 SAME; corpus-diff IDENTICAL.
